---
title: On Personal Digital Sovreignity
---

In Pratchett's Soul Music, we are greeted with a seemingly absurd scene where a
musician is unable to earn their keep playing, because it would be illegal for
them to play music without a membership at the Musician's Guild--who's fee they
could not afford--a wonderful Catch-22.
At first, it seems absurd that we'd give away so much of our autonomy.
And yet, we have given away such personal autonomy at least once this
century--in how we shape our oneline communities,
and we are being pushed with the force of half a trillion dollars, to do it again.


